) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 31.19 519.99 Td (2.) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 59.53 519.99 Td (\(1 point\) In SQL statements, constraint X foreign key \(Y\) references Z, what is Y?) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 59.53 505.82 Td (A\) The name of the foreign key columns in the current table) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 59.53 491.65 Td (B\) The name of the constraint) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 59.53 477.47 Td (C\) The name of the table to which the foreign resides) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 59.53 463.30 Td (D\) The name of the table from which the corresponding PK resides ) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 59.53 449.13 Td (E\) The name of primary key columns in the referenced table
) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 31.19 420.78 Td (3.) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 59.53 420.78 Td (\(1 point\) The difference between char\(100\) and varcharc2\(100\) is that, when actual text is less than 100) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 59.53 406.61 Td (characters, varchar2\(100\) will automatically save the remaining unused spaces for other uses. True or) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 59.53 392.43 Td (False) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 59.53 378.26 Td (A\) True) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 59.53 364.09 Td (B\) False
) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 31.19 335.74 Td (4.) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 59.53 335.74 Td (\(1 point\) What is not right about weak entities?) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 59.53 321.57 Td (A\) often used to model multivalued attributes) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 59.53 307.39 Td (B\) do not have a full UID themselves) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 59.53 293.22 Td (C\) must have 1:m relationships with a strong entity) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 59.53 279.05 Td (D\) cannot exist independently of a strong entity
) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 31.19 250.70 Td (5.) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 59.53 250.70 Td (\(1 point\) How is a gerund converted into a relational model?) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 59.53 236.53 Td (A\) ignore the gerund in the conversion) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 59.53 222.35 Td (B\) convert the gerund into a table without primary key) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 59.53 208.18 Td (C\) Convert the gerund into a table duplicate the primary keys of its both ends as a part of the composite) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 59.53 194.01 Td (foreign key for the gerund table) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 59.53 179.83 Td (D\) convert the gerund into a table and duplicate the primary keys of its both ends as a part of the) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 59.53 165.66 Td (composite primary key for the gerund table
) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 31.19 137.32 Td (6.) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 59.53 137.32 Td (\(1 point\) Which of the following is NOT required by the referential integrity rule #1) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 59.53 123.14 Td (A\) A foreign key column must have the same data type as the corresponding primary key column) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 59.53 108.97 Td (B\) A foreign key column must have the same field size as the corresponding primary key column) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 59.53 94.80 Td (C\) A foreign key column must have the optionality as the corresponding primary key column) Tj ET Q
q 0 g BT 59.53 80.62 Td (D\) None of the above
) Tj ET Q
